INT. ST. ALDWYN'S HOSPITAL - MAIN CORRIDOR - NIGHT

Victorian brick. Gas-lamp fittings bolted to bare wiring. Long and green and empty.

Rain hammers the tall windows.

Wind HOWLS through a cracked pane.

MARISOL VEGA, 30s, night nurse, pushes a squeaking cart. Her badge swings. Her eyes don't.

ON PHONE (TEXT): where r u

She doesn't answer. Pockets it.

DR. HELEN TEAGUE, 50s, surgeon, strides out of the stairwell. Coat open. Coffee in a shaking fist.

TEAGUE
You're late with the rounds.

MARISOL
You're early for the shift.

Teague shrugs. Drinks.

The radiators CLANK. Pipes GROAN. A lamp flickers.

Overhead, thunder ROLLS across the roof like furniture.

BRAM OKONKWO, 20s, orderly, jogs in from the east wing. Wet sneakers. Wide eyes.

BRAM
Ward Six. Bed nine. He's gone.

TEAGUE
Gone how?

BRAM
Gone gone. Bed's empty. Window's open.

Marisol and Teague trade a look. She nods. She nods.

Marisol's phone BUZZES.

ON PHONE (TEXT): pick up. now.

She answers. Speaker on.

JUNO (V.O.)
(filtered, tinny)
Marisol, tell me you're still in the building.

MARISOL
I'm in the corridor. With Teague.

JUNO (V.O.)
Is she wearing the grey coat?

Marisol looks. Teague looks down at her coat. Grey.

MARISOL
Yes.

JUNO (V.O.)
Then walk away from her. Slowly.

Teague sets her coffee down. Slowly.

TEAGUE
Who is that?

MARISOL
Nobody.

Pipes CLANK. The lamp DIES. Rain. Dark. A single emergency bulb hums red.

Bram steps back. Teague steps forward. Marisol steps between.

BRAM
Somebody tell me what's happening.

Nobody does.
